A vulnerability has been found in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/unitree_robotics:unitree_go2">Unitree Robotics Unitree Go2 up to 1.1.13/1.1.14.1/1.1.15.1</a> and classified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">problematic</a>. This affects the function <code>WebSocketClient.connect</code> of the file <em>websocket.py</em> of the component <em>chat_go</em>. Performing a manipulation results in improper certificate validation.

This vulnerability was named <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-115996">CVE-2026-115996</a>. The attack may be initiated remotely. There is no available exploit.

The vendor confirmed early: &quot;These issues were previously submitted by the researcher through our Security Response Center platform and are tracked internally as follows: Submission 990504 corresponds to our internal ticket #616 (Go2 chat_go WSS client disabled TLS server certificate validation, CWE-295).&quot;

A vulnerability has been found in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/travisun:opptrix">Travisun Opptrix 0.4.0</a> and classified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">problematic</a>. Affected is the function <code>Buffer.concat</code> of the file <em>/api/channels/webhook/</em> of the component <em>preParsing handler</em>. Performing a manipulation results in denial of service. This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer.

This vulnerability is identified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-115971">CVE-2026-115971</a>. The attack can be initiated remotely. Additionally, an exploit exists.

The project has been completely taken offline and deprecated. The project maintainer explains: &quot;The mentioned security risk was a design flaw that manifested primarily in local environments during earlier stages of version development. We previously addressed and resolved this specific risk; however, because the project was restricted to a small learning scope and the main versions were intended to run exclusively on localhost, the security fix was only pushed directly to our GitHub repository before it went private.&quot;

A vulnerability, which was classified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">critical</a>, was found in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/travisun:opptrix">Travisun Opptrix 0.4.0</a>. This impacts an unknown function of the file <em>/api/system-update/import</em> of the component <em>Import Endpoint</em>. Such manipulation leads to code injection. This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer.

This vulnerability is referenced as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-115970">CVE-2026-115970</a>. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. Furthermore, an exploit is available.

The project has been completely taken offline and deprecated. The project maintainer explains: &quot;The mentioned security risk was a design flaw that manifested primarily in local environments during earlier stages of version development. We previously addressed and resolved this specific risk; however, because the project was restricted to a small learning scope and the main versions were intended to run exclusively on localhost, the security fix was only pushed directly to our GitHub repository before it went private.&quot;

A vulnerability, which was classified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">critical</a>, has been found in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/travisun:opptrix">Travisun Opptrix 0.4.0</a>. This affects an unknown function of the file <em>/api/auth/setup</em> of the component <em>Schedule API</em>. This manipulation causes command injection. This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer.

The identification of this vulnerability is <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-115969">CVE-2026-115969</a>. It is possible to initiate the attack remotely. Furthermore, there is an exploit available.

