A vulnerability categorized as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">problematic</a> has been discovered in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/scada-lts">Scada-LTS 2.8.0</a>. Affected by this vulnerability is the function <code>HttpServletRequest.getParameter</code> of the file <em>AmChartValuesAPI.java</em> of the component <em>AmCharts Data API</em>. Executing a manipulation of the argument <em>ids</em> can lead to authorization bypass.

This vulnerability is handled as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-115803">CVE-2026-115803</a>. The attack can be executed remotely. Additionally, an exploit exists.

The vendor announces: &quot;At this moment we are working on new release with security enhancements which will be introduced to the community soon.&quot;

A vulnerability was found in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/kakao:khaiii">Kakao khaiii up to 0.4</a> and classified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">problematic</a>. The impacted element is the function <code>khaiii::nn::Linear::open</code> of the file <em>src/main/cpp/khaiii/nn/Linear.cpp</em> of the component <em>JSON Config File Handler</em>. The manipulation of the argument <em>hidden_dim/class_num</em> results in out-of-bounds read. This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer.

This vulnerability is reported as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-115801">CVE-2026-115801</a>. The attack requires a local approach. Moreover, an exploit is present.

The vendor explains: &quot;khaiii treats the resource directory (--rsc-dir) as trusted input, like a binary or a shared library. To use this defect, an attacker must already be able to write to that directory. With that access, an attacker can change the analysis results without this defect.&quot;
